1
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:06,080
Cui Yihang, can you

2
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,240
take one of me and Xing?

3
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:08,040
Sure.

4
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:09,680
Xing.

5
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,000
Let's ask Cui Yihang or Si

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,120
to take one for us both.

7
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:14,500
(Suggests a group photo)

8
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:16,360
Let's stand here.

9
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:17,960
- Okay.
- Is this alright?

10
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:18,840
Hmm.

11
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:20,640
Let's sit on the banana.

12
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:21,040
Okay.

13
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:26,380
(Smiles)

14
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,080
That smile.

15
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:28,040
Are you ready?

16
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:28,420
Okay.

17
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:29,400
Yes.

18
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,400
One, two, three.

19
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:35,680
Here.

20
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:37,440
Okay.

21
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:40,080
It's coming out.

22
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:43,240
This looks a little like

23
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:44,440
those photos

24
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,920
of our parents when they were young.

25
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:48,450
(Laughs)
Doesn't it look like that?

26
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:49,360
A little.

27
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:50,240
Actually yes.

28
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:51,280
With how I look.

29
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:52,720
This smile and pose

30
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:54,080
reminds me of my parents

31
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:55,680
back in the '80s

32
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:56,320
and '90s.

33
00:00:57,720 --> 00:00:58,360
Pretty

34
00:00:58,360 --> 00:00:59,960
but a little silly.

35
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:01,880
Just so happen

36
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:03,880
you've traveled back
to your school days today.

37
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:04,440
Right.

38
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:07,680
You look so beautiful in this.

39
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:08,700
(Praise)

40
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:10,560
He's fallen for her.

41
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,800
You look so beautiful in this.

42
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:16,840
This photo makes me

43
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:19,000
feel like you're way out of my league.

44
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:24,320
Like I want to get closer,
but I'm too afraid to.

45
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:25,200
How is it?

46
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,120
I said this photo makes me feel like

47
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:28,560
Xing is way out of my league.

48
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:30,240
(Major compliment)

49
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:30,960
You look so aloof.

50
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:32,400
Like I'm the one trying to reach you.

51
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:33,120
For real.

52
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:36,680
It really makes you look
out of my league.

53
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:41,040
He said it looks like the '80s or '90s.

54
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:41,920
Really.

55
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:42,600
The '80s or '90s.

56
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:44,000
When my parents fell in love.

57
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,520
You have this...

58
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:46,720
Kind, fatherly vibe, huh?

59
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:47,600
Yeah.

60
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,640
(Laughs)
Like you're out with your daughter.

61
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:50,080
Yeah.

62
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,720
This is hilarious.

63
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:52,680
Cool.

64
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:56,640
We'll use the sofa in my room.

65
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:57,160
We have a sofa.

66
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:00,320
It's freezing out there.

67
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:02,040
We'll just leave the door open.

68
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:02,680
It'll be fine.

69
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,000
I think you started strong,
then fell off.

70
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:11,040
Someone else asked you out.

71
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:11,560
I seriously...

72
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:13,680
I was about to lose it.

73
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:18,400
So tell me, busy bee.

74
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,880
If I want to ask you out,

75
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:20,960
how far ahead do I need to book you?

76
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:24,440
Boating today.

77
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,760
Plans tomorrow.

78
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:27,040
(Smiles)
What should...

79
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,520
Do you think I should wait here?

80
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,680
Do I just sit outside your door
and wait?

81
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,840
Compete. Don't you know how to compete?

82
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:37,960
Men who fight for a chance are the ones
who get a girl.

83
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:42,920
They haven't really

84
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:44,240
talked like this before.

85
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,560
They've been holding it all in.

86
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,320
Yes.

87
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:49,200
Everyone else fights
for their chance, but you...

88
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:52,480
They're all fighting outside the door.

89
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:53,240
And you?

90
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,320
You were hiding way over there.

91
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:55,320
I look over

92
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,760
and see you chatting happily

93
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:57,840
and having a great time.

94
00:02:58,640 --> 00:02:58,920
No.

95
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,000
When I went out,

96
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:01,680
I received two invitations.

97
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,280
Then...

98
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:04,400
Two invitations?

99
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:05,200
From who?

100
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:06,680
I can't tell you.

101
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:08,240
But I

102
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,560
actually wrote yours

103
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,600
and Liang Xiaoyu's.

104
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:13,600
You wrote two in one shot?

105
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:16,120
I wrote yours first.

106
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:18,720
But you wrote hers too.

107
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:19,960
I had to give out both.

108
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:20,800
Who else could I give it to?

109
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:21,400
I didn't know who else.

110
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:22,560
You could've given it to my roommate.

111
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:24,700
(Glances)

112
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:26,720
Cui Kaiyi?

113
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:27,200
Yes.

114
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,440
Chen Hewen didn't see that coming.

115
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,200
This is beyond him.

116
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:29,840
This is

117
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:30,680
too difficult for him.

118
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,760
Cui Kaiyi wrote to Zhao Xilun only

119
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,880
because she didn't want
to go the next day.

120
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:38,840
He's stunned.

121
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,080
He didn't think of this.

122
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:43,440
Such a well-behaved boy...

123
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:51,200
I just wanted to see what you'd do.

124
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:52,520
Me?

125
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,000
I wrote to you

126
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:54,960
and Liang Xiaoyu

127
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:55,960
because I only know you two

128
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:57,280
a little better than the others.

129
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:00,800
Because I only know you two

130
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,160
a little better than the others.

131
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:04,360
That came out wrong.

132
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:06,400
Oh no.

133
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,600
I don't even want to write your name now.

134
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:18,550
My gosh.

135
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:20,240
She's mad.

136
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,960
Because I wrote to Liang Xiaoyu?

137
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:27,160
Yes.

138
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:28,960
Now you don't want to write to me.

139
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:29,320
Yes.

140
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,360
Sha Yue'er wants to be the favorite.

141
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,400
But why?

142
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:45,480
Because I'm just the kind of person

143
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:46,680
who gets jealous easily

144
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:47,760
and petty like that.

145
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:48,600
Okay.

146
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,800
Now I know you better.

147
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:52,320
What's he doing?

148
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:54,040
He won't give in at all.

149
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:01,640
She keeps trying to find out,

150
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:03,640
but the answers
never seem to satisfy her.

151
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:05,520
What do they do now?

152
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:11,000
The funniest thing

153
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,360
about you is that...

154
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:16,080
She's about to cry.

155
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:20,860
(Turns away)

156
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:23,460
(Glances)
Comfort her.

157
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:26,320
No.

158
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:28,040
I think I was just expressing

159
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:29,840
what I wanted to say.

160
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:38,560
What's wrong?

161
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Go comfort her.

162
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,480
Why are you crying?

163
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,000
I'll get you

164
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:50,960
some tissues.

165
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:58,080
She's sad.

166
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:18,400
Did I go too far with what I said today?

167
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,000
Out there?

168
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:20,160
I'm sorry.

169
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:21,760
I really didn't mean to.

170
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:23,720
I was just trying

171
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:25,520
to express how I felt.

172
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:26,920
I didn't expect...

173
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:38,160
I'm sorry.

174
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:38,800
Really.

175
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,600
Here, wipe your tears.

176
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:47,340
(Wipes her tears)
I'm sorry.

177
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:53,320
Sorry. I'm really sorry.

178
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:55,120
Chen Hewen doesn't know what to do now.

179
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:58,040
You know, at first...

180
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,280
Go on.

181
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:05,520
What first drew me to you was

182
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:08,880
how direct you were at the dinner.

183
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:11,480
It made me think
you were really sincere.

184
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,320
The day you gave
the Master Kong Jasmine Coin,

185
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:15,160
you told me you only wanted
to get to know me.

186
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:16,480
But now you're asking me

187
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,760
why you can't get to know other people.

188
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:20,600
That you have the right
to meet other people.

189
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,040
Could it be

190
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,120
that's not what I meant?

191
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,200
What I actually said was

192
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,800
"If someone wants to get to know me,"

193
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:26,560
"I can't exactly reject them."

194
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,560
But you said
"Why don't you reject them?"

195
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,360
That's what you said.

196
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:32,680
You said the better you know someone,
the more you see their worth.

197
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:34,840
No, what I actually said was,

198
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,320
"Even as friends,"

199
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:37,720
"you'll see their good qualities."

200
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:39,880
They focused on different things.

201
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:43,200
What if I didn't give you an invitation?

202
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,320
Don't.

203
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:46,800
Be nice. Don't.

204
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:48,120
It's alright.

205
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,040
I accept it.

206
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:50,120
Don't do that!

207
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:51,400
It's fine.

208
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:53,440
I agree.

209
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:54,760
That's not okay.

210
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:55,440
Don't do this.

211
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:57,440
For real.

212
00:07:58,600 --> 00:07:59,640
Alright. Fine.

213
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:02,320
She...

214
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:05,400
Did she send

215
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:05,880
her invite?

216
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:06,360
Did she not?

217
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:06,920
Nope.

218
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:07,720
No.

219
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:14,320
Sha Yue'er.

220
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:16,320
Sha Yue'er?

221
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:19,080
Wait.

222
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:19,520
It's over.

223
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:23,520
Come on, dude.

224
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:24,760
What can he do now?

225
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,600
Sha Yue'er.

226
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,240
Wait.

227
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,640
How did the conversation
turn out like this?

228
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:23,960
Sha Yue'er is quite disappointed.

229
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:28,440
Hi.

230
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:28,960
You're back.

231
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:29,600
Cui Kaiyi.

232
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,600
Why are you on the floor?

233
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:31,240
What's happening?

234
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:32,160
I cried.

235
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:33,000
Why?

236
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:35,120
We fought,

237
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:37,400
and I cried.

238
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:38,440
What about him?

239
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,360
He was...

240
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,840
He first gave me a lecture

241
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:44,280
then tried to explain himself.

242
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:45,520
And I decided

243
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,240
not to give him my invitation card.

244
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,320
So you didn't give him one?

245
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:48,880
No.

246
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,560
Did you get his?

247
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:51,080
Yes.

248
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,320
But I don't want to give him mine.

249
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:57,720
I'm so sad.

250
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,080
Don't cry, sweetheart.

251
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:03,880
Don't cry.

252
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:05,640
A hug.

253
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:07,760
So sad.

254
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,560
What did you two talk about
to fight like that?

255
00:10:18,210 --> 00:10:18,600
My gosh.

256
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:38,820
(Exhausted)

257
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,440
Look what this did to Chaoyue.

258
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:41,640
You're worn out, huh?

259
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,520
Is my beard out?

260
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:48,800
I actually see

261
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:49,720
a lot of couples

262
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,760
that are like Chen Hewen

263
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:51,800
and Sha Yue'er.

264
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:54,680
When you fall for someone

265
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:55,800
who you know

266
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:57,360
isn't a good fit,

267
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:58,560
do you keep going

268
00:10:58,560 --> 00:10:59,720
or draw the line?

269
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:01,240
That's what I see

270
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,400
in the two of them.

271
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:04,080
First, I want to talk about Sha Yue'er.

272
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,240
In front of Chen Hewen,

273
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,520
she's already made

274
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:07,120
both her hidden thoughts

275
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:07,800
and conscious thoughts

276
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,200
perfectly clear to him.

277
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,880
She told him

278
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:12,960
to ask her out.

279
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:14,720
What that means was

280
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:15,400
she wants him.

281
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:16,800
She clearly told him

282
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:17,360
that she likes him.

283
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:18,720
She's not being unreasonable.

284
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:19,960
It's just that sometimes,

285
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:21,080
in a relationship,

286
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,440
you can have these

287
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,640
what we'd call

288
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:24,600
unreasonable

289
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:25,280
or what feels like

290
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:26,720
an overly emotional reaction.

291
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:28,560
It's usually because some need

292
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:30,400
isn't being met.

293
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,440
Yes.

294
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,400
Chen Hewen overlooks his own needs.

