to praise me

1454
00:51:33,040 --> 00:51:34,120
for this.

1455
00:51:34,120 --> 00:51:35,040
I may play it cool,

1456
00:51:35,040 --> 00:51:36,200
but I'm actually really happy.

1457
00:51:41,200 --> 00:51:42,000
The other day,

1458
00:51:42,360 --> 00:51:44,260
Cao Yiheng was going to make squid.

1459
00:51:44,260 --> 00:51:45,280
- It was really good.
- Was it good?

1460
00:51:46,240 --> 00:51:46,960
I didn't get to try any.

1461
00:51:46,960 --> 00:51:47,760
What a shame.

1462
00:51:49,560 --> 00:51:50,400
It's really not something

1463
00:51:50,400 --> 00:51:51,160
I know much about.

1464
00:51:51,160 --> 00:51:52,100
But I can learn.

1465
00:51:56,680 --> 00:51:57,360
It's okay.

1466
00:51:57,360 --> 00:51:58,200
I can make it with you.

1467
00:51:58,800 --> 00:52:00,160
Sure. We can figure out
a squid dish together.

1468
00:52:00,520 --> 00:52:01,000
Sure.

1469
00:52:06,200 --> 00:52:07,120
Should we have that?

1470
00:52:07,960 --> 00:52:08,800
I'll cut it up.

1471
00:52:09,280 --> 00:52:09,680
Okay.

1472
00:52:10,800 --> 00:52:12,080
Have you figured out what it looks like?

1473
00:52:17,760 --> 00:52:18,760
Like that lamp behind you.

1474
00:52:19,640 --> 00:52:20,280
A sea turtle.

1475
00:52:20,540 --> 00:52:22,260
(A Sea Turtle?)

1476
00:52:24,820 --> 00:52:25,820
(Applause)
Really?

1477
00:52:25,840 --> 00:52:27,000
Look, a sea turtle is shaped like this.

1478
00:52:27,000 --> 00:52:28,320
If its head is here,

1479
00:52:28,320 --> 00:52:29,320
its eyes would be right here,

1480
00:52:29,320 --> 00:52:31,000
and the rest of the green part

1481
00:52:32,240 --> 00:52:32,760
would be its head.

1482
00:52:32,760 --> 00:52:33,460
(So Serious)

1483
00:52:34,960 --> 00:52:35,680
I can see that.

1484
00:52:35,680 --> 00:52:36,820
You really have quite an imagination.

1485
00:52:36,820 --> 00:52:37,500
Doesn't it kind of look like one?

1486
00:52:38,260 --> 00:52:39,020
Doesn't it kind of look like one?

1487
00:52:39,800 --> 00:52:41,040
But then what's the white part?

1488
00:52:42,800 --> 00:52:43,720
Maybe the turtle's hat?

1489
00:52:47,160 --> 00:52:48,440
Liang Xiaoyu really knows
how to keep a conversation going.

1490
00:52:49,240 --> 00:52:50,160
He's getting shy.

1491
00:52:51,680 --> 00:52:52,440
Here, cut it.

1492
00:52:52,920 --> 00:52:53,400
Okay.

1493
00:52:54,760 --> 00:52:56,040
It's fine. Take your time.

1494
00:52:57,080 --> 00:52:57,640
Perfect.

1495
00:52:58,280 --> 00:52:58,880
Here.

1496
00:52:58,880 --> 00:52:59,600
Thanks.

1497
00:53:01,680 --> 00:53:03,000
Let's see if you like my recommendation.

1498
00:53:11,480 --> 00:53:11,880
First,

1499
00:53:12,600 --> 00:53:13,200
you get the yuzu.

1500
00:53:13,680 --> 00:53:14,880
The yuzu jelly gives you some tartness,

1501
00:53:14,880 --> 00:53:15,920
then the matcha brings some bitterness.

1502
00:53:15,920 --> 00:53:16,920
It goes from tart to bitter.

1503
00:53:18,680 --> 00:53:19,280
That's interesting.

1504
00:53:19,600 --> 00:53:20,160
It's good.

1505
00:53:20,600 --> 00:53:22,640
So I basically kept my promise

1506
00:53:23,200 --> 00:53:24,560
to let you try this.

1507
00:53:25,720 --> 00:53:26,680
You did. It's really good.

1508
00:53:40,480 --> 00:53:41,560
I'll pack up the rest.

1509
00:53:50,120 --> 00:53:52,240
I can tell your right arm
is more muscular.

1510
00:53:54,600 --> 00:53:55,120
Why?

1511
00:53:55,720 --> 00:53:57,000
Your right arm is a little bigger.

1512
00:53:59,240 --> 00:54:00,160
Definitely bigger than my left.

1513
00:54:02,120 --> 00:54:02,680
From playing sports.

1514
00:54:04,960 --> 00:54:06,840
I've been playing for quite a while.

1515
00:54:07,120 --> 00:54:08,720
No, I actually meant it

1516
00:54:08,720 --> 00:54:09,800
as a compliment

1517
00:54:09,800 --> 00:54:10,840
to your arms.

1518
00:54:10,840 --> 00:54:11,780
(Praise)

1519
00:54:12,360 --> 00:54:13,080
A compliment?

1520
00:54:14,280 --> 00:54:15,160
They're not exactly the same size.

1521
00:54:15,600 --> 00:54:17,640
But that just means
they're well-defined.

1522
00:54:19,520 --> 00:54:20,640
You really know what to say.

1523
00:54:21,480 --> 00:54:22,480
She's so good at this.

1524
00:54:28,080 --> 00:54:29,320
You seem different now

1525
00:54:29,320 --> 00:54:30,760
than you do in the Signal House.

1526
00:54:32,600 --> 00:54:33,240
Well, I...

1527
00:54:33,240 --> 00:54:34,280
It's like this.

1528
00:54:35,800 --> 00:54:36,760
The me you see in the house

1529
00:54:37,200 --> 00:54:38,440
is only one side of me.

1530
00:54:39,400 --> 00:54:40,160
There's a lot more

1531
00:54:40,960 --> 00:54:41,520
for you

1532
00:54:41,520 --> 00:54:43,000
to discover.

1533
00:54:45,080 --> 00:54:45,440
Okay.

1534
00:54:45,920 --> 00:54:47,160
I'm a gold miner.

1535
00:54:47,160 --> 00:54:48,820
(I'm a gold miner)

1536
00:54:49,480 --> 00:54:50,960
A gold miner.

1537
00:54:50,960 --> 00:54:52,600
I'm a gold miner.

1538
00:54:52,960 --> 00:54:54,360
I'm a gold miner.

1539
00:54:54,360 --> 00:54:57,300
(I'm a gold miner)

1540
00:54:58,000 --> 00:54:59,600
I guess I'm one as well.

1541
00:55:00,120 --> 00:55:01,400
Digging my way

1542
00:55:01,400 --> 00:55:02,280
into your heart.

1543
00:55:07,200 --> 00:55:09,400
I feel like I'm learning
just by watching them.

1544
00:55:16,200 --> 00:55:17,120
After watching this,

1545
00:55:17,120 --> 00:55:17,880
I feel like Chen Hewen

1546
00:55:17,880 --> 00:55:19,200
is a little seedling,

1547
00:55:19,560 --> 00:55:20,880
and Liang Xiaoyu

1548
00:55:20,880 --> 00:55:22,440
is like his greenhouse.

1549
00:55:22,440 --> 00:55:24,400
He can grow freely around her,

1550
00:55:24,400 --> 00:55:25,720
with all the sunshine

1551
00:55:25,720 --> 00:55:26,680
and water he needs.

1552
00:55:26,680 --> 00:55:27,760
And I think another reason

1553
00:55:27,760 --> 00:55:29,520
they connect so well

1554
00:55:29,520 --> 00:55:30,280
Liang Xiaoyu prefers

1555
00:55:30,280 --> 00:55:31,920
to get to know him first,

1556
00:55:31,920 --> 00:55:33,240
then give him time

1557
00:55:33,240 --> 00:55:33,760
to become curious

1558
00:55:33,760 --> 00:55:34,760
and learn more about her.

1559
00:55:36,920 --> 00:55:38,870
(Liang Xiaoyu: Gently takes the lead)
She's good at guiding things along.

1560
00:55:38,880 --> 00:55:40,560
She's soft-spoken,

1561
00:55:40,560 --> 00:55:41,880
and takes things at an easy pace.

1562
00:55:42,240 --> 00:55:42,920
And you can see

1563
00:55:42,920 --> 00:55:43,600
Chen Hewen

1564
00:55:43,600 --> 00:55:44,880
gradually matching her pace.

1565
00:55:44,880 --> 00:55:46,460
Liang Xiaoyu is just more mature.

1566
00:55:46,460 --> 00:55:46,880
Think about it.

1567
00:55:46,880 --> 00:55:48,040
They've spent quite some time together,

1568
00:55:48,040 --> 00:55:49,640
but she's only now
opening up about herself.

1569
00:55:49,640 --> 00:55:51,500
This was her first time opening up.

1570
00:55:51,500 --> 00:55:52,220
And it only happened

1571
00:55:52,220 --> 00:55:53,040
because Chen Hewen asked

1572
00:55:53,040 --> 00:55:53,880
about her.

1573
00:55:54,280 --> 00:55:55,120
This was the right moment

1574
00:55:55,120 --> 00:55:56,080
for Liang Xiaoyu

1575
00:55:56,080 --> 00:55:56,640
to share

1576
00:55:56,640 --> 00:55:57,640
her story.

1577
00:55:57,640 --> 00:55:58,240
And I think

1578
00:55:58,240 --> 00:55:59,280
hearing about her startup journey

1579
00:55:59,280 --> 00:56:00,480
probably made Chen Hewen

1580
00:56:00,480 --> 00:56:01,600
like her even more.

1581
00:56:02,600 --> 00:56:03,720
There was

1582
00:56:03,720 --> 00:56:04,480
something important

1583
00:56:04,480 --> 00:56:05,240
in what Liang Xiaoyu said.

1584
00:56:05,240 --> 00:56:06,120
For her,

1585
00:56:06,120 --> 00:56:07,080
the biggest difference

1586
00:56:07,080 --> 00:56:08,680
between a job and a career

1587
00:56:08,680 --> 00:56:09,600
is that with consulting,

1588
00:56:09,600 --> 00:56:10,600
people might see it

1589
00:56:10,600 --> 00:56:12,080
as a prestigious job.

1590
00:56:13,080 --> 00:56:14,160
But she wasn't happy.

1591
00:56:14,560 --> 00:56:15,840
So she chose something

1592
00:56:15,840 --> 00:56:16,840
that she herself

1593
00:56:16,840 --> 00:56:18,160
felt happier doing,

1594
00:56:18,160 --> 00:56:20,080
(Liang Xiaoyu: Choosing her own path)
instead of letting herself be defined

1595
00:56:20,320 --> 00:56:21,800
by other people's

1596
00:56:21,800 --> 00:56:22,680
expectations of her.

1597
00:56:22,680 --> 00:56:23,160
They assume

1598
00:56:23,160 --> 00:56:24,480
that as a Tsinghua graduate,

1599
00:56:24,480 --> 00:56:25,640
she should

1600
00:56:25,640 --> 00:56:26,260
join a Fortune 500 company

1601
00:56:26,260 --> 00:56:26,920
and build her career there.

1602
00:56:26,920 --> 00:56:27,800
That's what people expect.

1603
00:56:27,800 --> 00:56:29,560
She chose to focus on
what she truly wanted.

1604
00:56:30,800 --> 00:56:31,720
When you've

1605
00:56:31,720 --> 00:56:32,680
just graduated from college

1606
00:56:32,680 --> 00:56:33,680
and you're still unsure

1607
00:56:33,680 --> 00:56:34,480
where you fit

1608
00:56:34,480 --> 00:56:36,080
in your career

1609
00:56:36,080 --> 00:56:37,160
or in society,

1610
00:56:37,160 --> 00:56:38,560
a "job" can actually be

1611
00:56:38,560 --> 00:56:40,180
(Starting out and finding your way)
the first step toward a career.

1612
00:56:40,200 --> 00:56:41,840
As you learn how things work

1613
00:56:41,840 --> 00:56:42,600
and start

1614
00:56:42,600 --> 00:56:43,760
to understand

1615
00:56:43,760 --> 00:56:45,440
what you can do in your role,

1616
00:56:45,440 --> 00:56:46,920
you begin to develop

1617
00:56:46,920 --> 00:56:48,600
a sense of who you are.

1618
00:56:49,160 --> 00:56:51,760
And through that experience,

1619
00:56:51,760 --> 00:56:53,720
you can gradually
build a clearer picture

1620
00:56:53,720 --> 00:56:54,720
of the life

1621
00:56:54,720 --> 00:56:56,280
you want for yourself.

1622
00:56:56,280 --> 00:56:57,440
That's what Liang Xiaoyu did.

1623
00:56:57,440 --> 00:56:58,480
Through each job experience,

1624
00:56:58,480 --> 00:56:59,040
she gradually

1625
00:56:59,040 --> 00:56:59,920
found a career

1626
00:56:59,920 --> 00:57:01,850
(Passion grows through experience)
she truly cared about

1627
00:57:01,880 --> 00:57:02,800
and became passionate about it.

1628
00:57:04,520 --> 00:57:05,840
Young people today

1629
00:57:05,840 --> 00:57:06,520
actually tend to be very clear

1630
00:57:06,520 --> 00:57:07,520
about the choices

1631
00:57:07,520 --> 00:57:08,640
they want to make.

1632
00:57:09,480 --> 00:57:10,880
All right,

1633
00:57:10,880 --> 00:57:12,840
let's move on to the next date.

1634
00:57:13,880 --> 00:57:15,720
(Next episode)
Anything make you happy today?

1635
00:57:15,720 --> 00:57:17,520
Seeing you was the best part of my day.

1636
00:57:18,320 --> 00:57:19,120
Oh my gosh!

1637
00:57:19,120 --> 00:57:20,840
I've actually been looking forward

1638
00:57:20,840 --> 00:57:22,360
to some time alone with you.

1639
00:57:23,280 --> 00:57:24,880
You two are flirting with us now.

1640
00:57:24,880 --> 00:57:26,400
My parents are both great cooks.

1641
00:57:26,400 --> 00:57:27,800
When you come over,

1642
00:57:27,800 --> 00:57:28,440
you can try their cooking.

1643
00:57:29,600 --> 00:57:30,760
Something to look forward to next year.

1644
00:57:31,040 --> 00:57:31,590
Okay.

1645
00:57:32,400 --> 00:57:33,880
Next year, we'll go to Cui Kaiyi's place

1646
00:57:33,880 --> 00:57:34,720
and celebrate the New Year together.

1647
00:57:34,720 --> 00:57:35,960
That's our little sunshine.

1648
00:57:36,760 --> 00:57:37,520
What are we doing?

1649
00:57:39,880 --> 00:57:40,880
This is terrifying.

1650
00:57:40,880 --> 00:57:42,760
What if I get scared halfway through

1651
00:57:42,760 --> 00:57:43,640
and want to get off?

1652
00:57:43,640 --> 00:57:45,400
Once you start, there's no turning back.

1653
00:57:47,480 --> 00:57:48,440
It's okay. I'll catch you.

1654
00:57:50,520 --> 00:57:51,920
Zhao Xilun, here I come!

1655
00:57:51,920 --> 00:57:52,880
Don't be scared. I'm here.

1656
00:57:53,720 --> 00:57:55,080
I hope we can both
be braver in the future.

1657
00:57:55,080 --> 00:57:55,760
(Holding onto each other)

1658
00:57:55,760 --> 00:57:57,200
This is for you.

1659
00:57:58,300 --> 00:57:59,200
Oh my gosh!

1660
00:57:59,240 --> 00:58:00,520
That's a smart move!

1661
00:58:00,520 --> 00:58:01,280
In the Signal House,

1662
00:58:01,280 --> 00:58:02,520
what would you say was

1663
00:58:02,520 --> 00:58:04,400
your happiest moment or day?

1664
00:58:04,400 --> 00:58:05,160
(Confidential)

1665
00:58:05,160 --> 00:58:06,080
Don't read it out loud.

1666
00:58:06,740 --> 00:58:07,920
(Blushing)

1667
00:58:07,920 --> 00:58:08,760
I've always felt...

1668
00:58:08,760 --> 00:58:09,500
(Confidential)

1669
00:58:11,400 --> 00:58:12,830
Oh my gosh!

1670
00:58:12,840 --> 00:58:14,320
That scored major points.

1671
00:58:16,040 --> 00:58:17,280
Chen Hewen needs to step it up.

1672
00:58:17,480 --> 00:58:18,800
Now I'm a little upset.

1673
00:58:19,400 --> 00:58:19,800
Uh...

1674
00:58:20,360 --> 00:58:21,200
So lonely.

1675
00:58:23,160 --> 00:58:24,040
What's going on?

